      "note": "<b>Cómo funciona:</b> <b>tarjetas</b> <ico-clone></ico-clone>, <b>elegir respuestas</b> <ico-comments></ico-comments>, <b>unir</b> <ico-link></ico-link>, <b>escucha</b> <ico-headphones></ico-headphones>, <b>completar</b> <ico-filepen></ico-filepen> y <b>ordenar</b> <ico-puzzle></ico-puzzle>. <ico-check></ico-check> CHECK donde lo veas.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>1 · DO / DOES</b> <span class='es'>— preguntas con verbos</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "Do you like music?",
              "sp": "¿Te gusta la música? — con I / you / we / they."
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, I do. / No, I don't.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No."
            },
            {
              "en": "Does she work here?",
              "sp": "¿Ella trabaja aquí? — con he / she / it."
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b>En español basta con la entonación</b> («¿Te gusta el café?»). En inglés hace falta <b>do</b>: <s class='x'>You like coffee?</s> → <span class='ok'>Do you like coffee?</span><br>Y después de <b>does</b> el verbo va sin -s, igual que con have: <s class='x'>Does she works?</s> → <span class='ok'>Does she work?</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>2 · PREGUNTAS CON BE</b> <span class='es'>— sin do</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "Are you a student?",
              "sp": "¿Eres estudiante? — <b>be</b> pasa adelante."
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, I am. / No, I'm not.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No."
            },
            {
              "en": "Is Tom from Canada?",
              "sp": "¿Tom es de Canadá?"
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "<ico-warn></ico-warn> be y do no se mezclan",
              "body": "<s class='x'>Do you are a student?</s> → <span class='ok'>Are you a student?</span><br><s class='x'>Are you like music?</s> → <span class='ok'>Do you like music?</span><br>La respuesta corta no se contrae: <s class='x'>Yes, I'm.</s> → <span class='ok'>Yes, I am.</span>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>3 · CAN</b> <span class='es'>— saber o poder hacer algo</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "I can cook.",
              "sp": "Sé cocinar."
            },
            {
              "en": "I can't swim.",
              "sp": "No sé nadar."
            },
            {
              "en": "Can you swim?",
              "sp": "¿Sabes nadar?"
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, I can. / No, I can't.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b>Can no lleva to, ni do, ni -s:</b> <s class='x'>I can to swim.</s> → <span class='ok'>I can swim.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <s class='x'>Do you can swim?</s> → <span class='ok'>Can you swim?</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <s class='x'>He cans</s> → <span class='ok'>He can</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>4 · WHAT, WHERE, WHEN…</b> <span class='es'>— palabras de pregunta</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "Where do you live?",
              "sp": "¿Dónde vives? — <b>Where</b> = lugar."
            },
            {
              "en": "What do you do?",
              "sp": "¿A qué te dedicas? — pregunta por tu trabajo: <i>I'm an engineer.</i>"
            },
            {
              "en": "When is your class?",
              "sp": "¿Cuándo es tu clase? — <b>When</b> = día u hora."
            },
            {
              "en": "Who is she?",
              "sp": "¿Quién es ella? — <b>Who</b> = persona."
            },
            {
              "en": "How old are you?",
              "sp": "¿Cuántos años tienes? — <b>How</b> = cómo; <b>How old</b> = edad."
            },
            {
              "en": "Why do you study English? Because…",
              "sp": "¿Por qué…? Porque… — en inglés son dos palabras distintas."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "<ico-bulb></ico-bulb> El orden de la pregunta",
              "body": "palabra de pregunta + <code>do / does</code> + persona + verbo<br><span class='ok'>Where do you live?</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span class='ok'>What does she do?</span><br>Con be: palabra de pregunta + <code>be</code> + persona: <span class='ok'>Where are you from?</span><br><s class='x'>Where you live?</s> <s class='x'>What she does?</s>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
